From 051a535a69999e5b4fcaf2cb12f562371d4d8530 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] prompt: recursively splice @path imports in context files

Crush loads context files (CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/CRUSH.md, etc.) but passes
their contents to the model verbatim, so a `@path` reference written inside
one is literal text. This adds Claude-Code-compatible `@`-import: a line that
is exactly `@path` (leading whitespace allowed) is replaced by the referenced
file's contents, recursively.

MVP semantics: `~` is expanded; a relative path resolves against the importing
file's directory; recursion is capped at 5 hops; cycles are guarded via a
visited-set; an unreadable/missing target or a mid-line `@mention` is left as
literal text. Implemented as a small helper called from processFile, so every
loaded context file gets expansion and nothing else is touched.

Carried as a local patch for runCrushInContainer (git am at image-build time).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
